          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "освещать (osveshchát) — \"to report on, to cover (in the news); to light up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Газеты широко освещали эту историю. Gazéty shirokó osveshcháli étu istóriyu. The newspapers covered this story widely."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective осветить (osvetít), я освещу. First sense: лампа освещает комнату — the lamp lights the room."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "освещать (osveshchát) is built on о- and свет \"light\", an inherited Slavic word (Proto-Slavic světŭ), with -щ-, the Church Slavonic shape -свещ- (native Russian has ч, as in свеча): to throw light on."
            }
          ]
        },
