              "text": "тираж (tirázh) — \"a print run, a circulation; a lottery draw\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "У этой газеты большой тираж. U étoy gazéty bolshóy tirázh. This newspaper has a large circulation."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine; the stress moves to the ending: тиража, тиражи. Выиграть в тираже — to win in a lottery draw."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "тираж (tirázh) was borrowed from French tirage \"a printing; a drawing of lots\" (EtymDB). The French noun is usually traced to tirer \"to draw, to pull\", as copies are drawn off a press and numbers out of a drum; EtymDB lists no parent for tirage itself."
            }
          ]
        },
